169 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (we created a global variable pi. We also created a function square\(\) that does not take any argument as its input. However, it can change the value of pi because it is a global variable, and we could access pi in this function. In the main function, we printed the initial value of pi, i.e. 3.140000. Then, we incremented the value of pi and printed the updated value, i.e. 4.140000. Finally, we called the square\(\) function. Because the new value of pi was 4.14, the square\(\) function squared 4.14 and we got 17.139603 as the new value of pi.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
